Provides: firmware-xiaomi-marble (= ${source:Version})
Description: Firmware for Xiaomi POCO F5 / Redmi Note 12 Turbo (marble)
 Proprietary signed firmware blobs for the marble mainline Linux port:
 ADSP, SLPI, modem and IPA, Adreno 725 (zap / SQE / GMU), Iris VPU,
 WCN6855 Wi-Fi (ath11k board files) and Bluetooth, audio topology and
 speaker amplifier tuning, and the hexagonrpcd sensor registry.
 .
 Install paths follow the postmarketOS firmware-xiaomi-marble aport,
 adapted to UsrMerge: /usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8475/xiaomi/marble,
 /usr/lib/firmware/qcom, /usr/lib/firmware/ath11k and
 /usr/lib/firmware/qca, plus /usr/share/qcom/hexagonfs.
 .
 btqca asks for the wcn-prefixed Bluetooth names on WCN6855
 (drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c: "qca/wcnhpbtfw%02x.tlv" and "wcnhpnv..."),
 while the upstream tree only ships qca/hp*. debian/rules creates those
 links, which is the only place the names are adapted.
 .
 Proprietary firmware (c) Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and Xiaomi Inc.
 Device redistribution only.
